<title>UK: Prudential shares dip on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Prudential shares dip on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British insurance giant Prudential Corp Plc slipped on Monday on a round of profit-taking after recent gains, traders said.</p>
<p>By 1345 GMT, shares were down 13 pence at 585-1/2 pence, slightly above a low of 580 pence.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the shares were overextended and now we're seeing a bit of profit-taking,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Prudential shares had risen around 40 pence in two weeks to close on Friday at 598-1/2 pence.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
</text>
